## 6 BEACH OPERATIONAL REQUIREMENTS

### 6.1  Beach Information


6.1.1 The information shall be displayed in a minimum of three languages, preferably English, Hindi and the local language. The displayed information shall be legible and visible to the naked eye. All structural materials used in display boards shall be corrosion free, adequately secured, and of sufficient strength to withstand environmental conditions such as high winds, heavy rainfall, intense sunlight and saline air. The BMC shall ensure that the following information is made available on-site to all stakeholders through various communication mediums such as digital displays, boards, signage, mobile applications or any other innovative means.


#### 6.1.2 Information about the Beach

The BMC shall display the following information about the beach at prominent and accessible locations throughout the beach area:

- a) Physical — Dimensions of the beach, as defined in 3.1;
- b) Historical — Any historical importance associated with the beach and its surrounding area;
- c) Ecological —  Information on ecological importance associated critical information;
- d) Economic — Details of any economic activities or services at the beach and their relevance to the beach users;
- e) Carrying Capacity — Maximum carrying capacity of the beach to accommodate visitors; and
- f) Weather Conditions — Information on seasonal variations and prevailing weather conditions.

