#### 6.1.3  Beach Layout Map


6.1.3.1 The BMC shall ensure that an accessible beach layout map is displayed at a prominent location, preferably near the beach entrance for visitor information.


6.1.3.2 The BMC shall monitor and maintain the beach layout map and associated information boards, including periodic updates in case of changes in facilities, operating zones, or other relevant elements. The beach layout map shall clearly indicate designated zones, landmarks, and facilities, including but not limited to the following:

- a) Locations of beach information board;
- b) Lifeguard stations along with hours of operation;
- c) First aid stations and beach officer posts;
- d) Emergency contact details;
- e) Drinking water stations;
- f) Demarcated bathing areas and safe swimming zones;
- g) Changing rooms and shower areas;
- h) Watchtower(s);
- j) Water sampling locations;
- k) Designated parking zones (for vehicles such as bicycles, motorcycles, cars, including electric charging stations);
- m) Restroom facilities;
- n) Food and Beverage (F&B) facilities;
- p) Waste bins with clear multilingual signage for waste segregation;
- q) Accessible and demarcated shaded seating areas;




- r) Solid waste management plant;
- s) Solar power plant (if available on-site);
- t) Grey water treatment plant;
- u) Local emergency assembly points;
- v) Entry/exit points;
- w) Dead coral reef rocks sites and their
ecological significance (wherever applicable);

- y) Turtle nesting sites (wherever applicable);
- z) Information on jellyfish bloom season (wherever applicable); and
aa) Archaeological sites, reserve forest, and

other protected areas (wherever applicable).

