#### 6.1.4 Environment and Ecology

The BMC shall ensure that information on environment and ecology of the beach is prominently displayed using various communication mediums such as information board, digital displays, mobile applications and signage. The information shall be accurate, up-to date, legible and easy to understand by the visitors. The information shall include, but not be limited to, the following:

- a) Ecotourism Activities — Sustainable tourism activities at or near the beach such as guided nature walk, birdwatching tours, educational programs focused on the local ecosystem;
- b) Bathing Water Quality — Details of quality of bathing water at marked locations, along with the date of the most recent testing. This information shall be updated regularly, ideally daily or as frequently as testing is conducted. The display shall indicate whether bathing is recommended or not, based on the latest test report;
- c) Tidal Information — Accurate and up-to- date tidal information, including high and
