#### 6.1.5 Code of Conduct for Beach Use


6.1.5.1 The BMC shall develop, implement and maintain a comprehensive code of conduct and maintain records to promote sustainable, safe, and responsible use of the beach while ensuring environmental protection. The document of the code of conduct and its revisions shall be maintained.


6.1.5.2 The code of conduct shall be prominently displayed at key locations across the beach, including entrances, information boards, and key facilities, and shall be effectively communicated to all visitors. The code of conduct shall include, but not be limited to, the following key provisions:

- a) Beach operational timings;
- b) Prohibited activities such as consumption or possession of alcohol or drug, smoking, littering, dumping of waste, fishing, camping, cooking, use of fireworks, use of single-use plastics, and excessive noise;
- c) Parking of vehicles only at designated parking zones;



- d) Restrictions on recreational activities, as defined by the BMC;
- e) Prohibition of motorized vehicles on the beach area;
- f) Ban on spitting within the beach premises;
- g) Mandatory compliance with instructions issued by the BMC authorized security and safety personnel, and with announcements made by the control room or authorized persons;
- h) Prohibition on causing damage to environmentally sensitive areas and ecosystems;
- j) Safeguarding public infrastructure available on the beach area;
- k) Compliance to all the notices issued or displayed at the beach area;
- m) Mechanisms for submitting feedback or grievances to the BMC; and
- n) Restrictions on shops and vendors in accordance with the BMC guidelines.

6.1.5.3 The code of conduct shall align with all the applicable legal and regulatory frameworks.

