#### 6.2.2 Use of Eco-Friendly Transport

To promote sustainable mobility and minimize the environmental impact of transportation, the BMC shall implement the following measures:

- a) Inclusion of the environmental advantages of adopting eco-friendly transportation modes in awareness programs to educate all stakeholders, including visitors, vendors, and transport operators;
- b) Display of information regarding availability of public transport services, designated bicycle routes, pedestrian friendly pathways, and electric vehicle (EV) charging stations;
- c) Development of designated parking areas with dedicated EV charging facilities, situated at strategic and convenient locations, preferably within or adjacent to the parking zones, to encourage the use of electric vehicles;
- d) Preparation of a comprehensive traffic management plan in coordination with the state transport department, outlining movement control, drop-off/pick-up points, and emergency vehicle access. The plan shall be enforced by the beach manager in collaboration with the local traffic police, and supported by proper directional signage and visitor guidance systems; and
- e) Coordination with state transport authorities and private transport operators for the operation of eco-friendly shuttle
