#### 6.4.3 Beach Cleaning

The BMC shall maintain cleanliness and environmental hygiene throughout the beach area and its surroundings, including access routes, parking lots, and walkways. The BMC shall take the following measures to ensure beach cleaning:

- a) Preparation and implementation of a regular cleaning schedule for all designated beach zones, with regular monitoring to ensure effective execution;
- b) Provisions of well-maintained colour coded waste bins (for general waste, recyclables, and organic waste) securely placed at key locations such as entrances, exits, restrooms/toilets, and high traffic areas;
- c) Protection of local flora and fauna, particularly in ecologically sensitive zones, such as nesting areas where turtles may have buried eggs;
- d) Obtaining necessary prior permissions or approvals from relevant authorities before initiating cleaning operations in protected zones;
- e) Prohibition of the use of insecticides or chemical agents for cleaning beach sand or the surrounding environment to promote eco-friendly and biodegradable cleaning products;
- f) Regular cleaning of storm water outlets and surrounding areas, especially during heavy rainfall, to prevent accumulation of waste and pollutants;
- g) Removal of invasive plant species and prioritization of protection and restoration of native vegetation to enhance the local coastal ecosystem;
- h) Establishment of protocols for waste management during and after public




events, community gatherings, or natural disasters;

- j) Organize regular beach clean-up campaigns in collaboration with local communities, schools, Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs), and other relevant stakeholders;
- k) Maintenance of the beach area free from solid waste, including pebbles, garbage, marine litter, discarded plastics, fishing gear, and other debris. The records of all cleaning activities shall be maintained; and
- m) Disposal of all collected waste through scientifically sound and environmentally sustainable methods, in compliance with local and national regulations.

#### 6.4.4 Solid Waste Disposal

The BMC shall establish and implement a schedule for daily collection, segregation and disposal of solid waste by the designated agency (for example, Municipal Corporation/Public Health Engineering Department/Gram Panchayat). The beach manager shall ensure that solid waste is disposed of as per the established schedule and in accordance with the provisions of the Solid Waste Management Rules, 2016.

