### 6.6 Safety and Security


#### 6.6.1 Deployment of Lifeguards

The BMC shall ensure the deployment of trained and certified lifeguards during the operational hours of the beach. In addition, the BMC shall ensure the following:

- a) A minimum ratio of one lifeguard per 100 m shall be maintained;
- b) Lifeguard stations with a designated coordinator shall be established at strategic locations and equipped with standard lifesaving gears and communication tools;
- c) Conduct regular emergency drills in coordination with the beach manager to ensure that lifeguards and beach staff are adequately prepared to respond to incidents such as drownings, injuries, or hazardous situations;
- d) A comprehensive emergency response plan shall be prepared, documented, and implemented, including clearly defined protocols for coordination with local authorities and relevant agencies during emergencies;
- e) A training schedule for all lifeguards shall be prepared, documented, and implemented, ensuring that each lifeguard undergoes skill enhancement training at least once annually. Such training shall be conducted by certified lifeguard trainers to ensure continuous proficiency in lifesaving competencies; and
- f) Prepare document, and implement a training schedule for all the lifeguard, ensuring that each lifeguard undergoes skill enhancement training at least once annually. These training shall be conducted by certified lifeguard trainers to ensure continuous proficiency lifesaving competencies.

#### 6.6.2 Watchtower

The BMC shall establish watchtowers at strategically selected locations across the beach area to ensure effective surveillance and prompt emergency response. The compliance with the following requirements shall be ensured:

- a) Watchtowers shall be positioned to provide a clear, unobstructed 360° view of the beach and surrounding areas, enabling continuous monitoring of visitor activities and early detection of potential hazards;




- b) Each watchtower shall be manned by designated and trained personnel who are responsible for continuous surveillance and coordination during beach operational hours;
- c) Watchtowers shall be equipped with reliable communication systems, including mobile phones, wireless radios, or other equivalent electronic devices, to facilitate real-time communication with rescue teams, medical support staff, and other lifeguards;
- d) The design of the watchtowers shall ensure safety, stability, and resilience to weather conditions using durable and sustainable materials. The access to watchtowers shall be allowed only to authorized personnel;
- e) Signage indicating the location and function of the watchtowers shall be clearly displayed for public awareness; and
- f) Periodic drills shall be conducted at regular intervals to assess readiness and communication efficiency. The records of such drills shall be maintained.

