#### 6.7.12 Beach Flags


6.7.12.1 The Beach Flag shall indicate the operational classification of the beach (Class I, II or III) based on the level of compliance to the requirements of this standard. This flag shall serve as a visual representation of the beach’s adherence to the applicable requirements of this standard.


6.7.12.2 In the event of non-compliance with any of the requirements corresponding to the declared operational class of the beach, the beach manager shall immediately remove or lower the beach flag until full compliance is restored.


6.7.12.3 In order to ensure visitor awareness, beach classification visibility, and operational control, the BMC shall ensure the display of designated flags and signage within the beach premises. The BMC shall display the following flags/signage at designated beach areas.

- a) Flags at prominent location within the beach area:
- 1) National Flag; and
- 2) Beach Flag (as certified by the certification agency).
- b) Flags/signage at appropriate locations across the beach:
- 1) Swimming zone;
- 2) Water sports zone;
- 3) No water sports area;
- 4) Dangerous marine life in water;
- 5) Warning flags;
- 6) Caution flag;
- 7) High danger area; and
