#### 6.7.13 Signage Boards and Placards

To ensure safety, accessibility, awareness, and effective guidance for beach visitors, the BMC shall install   signage  boards/placards  across  the  beach



area. In this regard, the following requirements shall be met:

- a) Signage boards/placards shall be installed at all critical points, including entrances, parking areas, changing rooms, shower areas, restrooms, eco huts, children’s parks, watchtowers, accessible pathways, and high-risk zones. All signage shall be clearly visible, durable, and positioned at an accessible height;
- b) Each board/placard shall provide clear, concise, and multilingual information, where applicable, covering key details such as:
- 1) Safety instructions and emergency contact information;
- 2) Bathing and swimming zones;
- 3) Prohibited activities;
- 4) Environmental conservation messages;
- 5) Locations of key amenities and services; and
- 6) Accessibility features and guidelines.
- c) The BMC shall install signage boards/ placards declaring the beach as a plastic free zone at prominent locations and ensure the following provisions:
- 1) Placards shall be installed at entry/exit points, parking areas, food and beverage facilities, and other high-footfall locations to ensure maximum visibility to the beach visitors;
- 2) The messages on the placards shall be clear, concise, and multilingual, encouraging visitors to avoid single use plastics, dispose of waste responsibly, and carry reusable alternatives (for example cloth bags, bottles, containers); and
- 3) Where feasible, the placards should include QR codes or links directing users to more information on marine conservation, and sustainable tourism practices.
- d) Signage boards and placards shall be made of sustainable and weather-resistant materials, and designed to complement the natural aesthetics of the beach environment; and
- e) The BMC shall ensure that all signage boards and placards are regularly
inspected, updated, and maintained to remain legible, clean and secure at all times.


#### 6.7.14  Information and Technological Infrastructure

To facilitate efficient operations, coordination, and information access at the beach area, the BMC shall ensure the necessary IT infrastructure, including desktops/laptops and internet connectivity, with the following provisions:

- a) Assess and determine the operational requirements for laptops/desktops, Wi-Fi and LAN connectivity based on the scale of operations, staff and digital service needs;
- b) Adequate provisions for Wi-Fi and LAN infrastructure with sufficient bandwidth to support essential digital functions, such as emergency communications, monitoring systems, visitor information services, and coordination with external agencies; and
- c) The internet network shall have coverage across operational zones, including control rooms, administrative offices, and other designated areas.

