## ANNEX C

(Clause 4.2)

COMPOSITION OF BEACH MANAGEMENT COMMITTEE

C-1 An indicative composition of the Beach Management Committee is prescribed as below:

- a) Chairperson — The District Collector shall serve as the Chairperson. In the absence of the Chairperson, an officer may be nominated by the District Collector, not below the rank of Additional District Magistrate or Sub- Divisional Officer to act as the Chairperson;
- b) Secretary;
- c) Treasurer;
- d) A representative from the District Coastal Zone Management Committee (DCZMC); and
- e) Six additional members.
C-2 The six additional members should be included in the BMC among representatives of the following organizations/departments:

- a) Municipal Corporation/Public Health Engineering Department (PHED);
- b) Beach Manager;
- c) Forest Department;
- d) State Tourism Department;
- e) Central/State Pollution Control Board/Committee;
- f) State/National Disaster Response Force;
- g) State Fishery Department;
- h) Local NGO;
- j) State Transport Department;
- k) Gram Panchayat/ Community representatives;
- m) Hotelier/Restaurant Association;
- n) Local Vendor Association;
- p) Lifeguard;
- q) Consumer organization;
- r) Police/Marine Police;
- s) Gram Panchayat; and
- t) Local Fisher’s Representative;
C-3 The selection of six members should be decided based on local, social, ecological, economical and other significant concerns.
